        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Gnosticism</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 150 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Origin</span><span class="info-stat-val">the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> world, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandria">Alexandria</a> central to its birth; the origins cannot be traced exactly and are disputed, and the systems were fully developed by the mid-2nd century</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founder or early teachers</span><span class="info-stat-val">none: a collection of groups and teachers, among them Valentinus (c. 100 – c. 180), Basilides of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandria">Alexandria</a> and Marcion, rather than one founder</span></div>
